CardDecks.register({"id":"nocturne-gothic","name":"Nocturne Cathedral Tarot","shortName":"Gothic Tarot","order":1,"ready":false,"gallery":"/decks/gothic","back":"/cards/gothic/back.webp","description":"An original 78-card journey through moonlit cathedrals, silver shadows, and quiet courage.","cards":[{"id":"the-fool","n":0,"rn":"0","name":"The Fool","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["beginnings","trust","possibility"],"up":"A new passage opens before you. Take one honest step with curiosity, carrying enough care to make freedom sustainable.","rev":"Pause at the threshold if excitement has outrun preparation. A small plan can protect the adventure without extinguishing it.","symbolism":"The moonlit crossing is a threshold between the familiar and the unknown; the small companion embodies instinct that travels with us.","aff":["I can begin before I know the whole path."],"question":"What first step could you take with both wonder and care?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-fool.webp","alt":"The Fool: The moonlit crossing is a threshold between the familiar and the unknown; the small companion embodies instinct that travels with us.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-magician","n":1,"rn":"I","name":"The Magician","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["intention","skill","agency"],"up":"Your tools are already within reach. Bring attention, practical skill, and clear intention together to turn an idea into an action.","rev":"Scattered attention or impressive promises may conceal a missing step. Check what you can actually do and commit to one grounded action.","symbolism":"The cathedral becomes a workshop of will, where the four suits link imagination with the material world.","aff":["My attention gives form to possibility."],"question":"Which resource have you overlooked because it feels ordinary?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-magician.webp","alt":"The Magician: The cathedral becomes a workshop of will, where the four suits link imagination with the material world.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-high-priestess","n":2,"rn":"II","name":"The High Priestess","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["intuition","silence","mystery"],"up":"Leave a little space around the question. Quiet observation and the knowledge of your body may reveal what hurried explanations miss.","rev":"Silence may have become avoidance, or outside voices may be drowning your own. Seek facts where needed and give your inner response time to arrive.","symbolism":"A watchful feline priestess inhabits the moonlit sanctuary, guarding the threshold between spoken knowledge and felt understanding.","aff":["I listen before I name."],"question":"What do you notice when you stop trying to force an answer?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-high-priestess.webp","alt":"The High Priestess: A watchful feline priestess inhabits the moonlit sanctuary, guarding the threshold between spoken knowledge and felt understanding.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-empress","n":3,"rn":"III","name":"The Empress","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["nurture","creativity","abundance"],"up":"Care is a creative practice. Feed the project, relationship, or body that needs patient attention and let growth follow its own season.","rev":"Overgiving or neglect may be draining the ground you depend on. Restore nourishment and boundaries before asking for more growth.","symbolism":"The abbey garden brings living abundance into old stone, showing how tenderness can reclaim a place shaped by loss.","aff":["I make room for life to flourish."],"question":"What would nourishment look like in one practical choice today?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-empress.webp","alt":"The Empress: The abbey garden brings living abundance into old stone, showing how tenderness can reclaim a place shaped by loss.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-emperor","n":4,"rn":"IV","name":"The Emperor","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["structure","stewardship","boundaries"],"up":"Build a dependable frame for what matters. Fair boundaries and accountable leadership make room for others to feel secure.","rev":"Control may be substituting for trust, or uncertainty may be keeping useful structure away. Choose a rule that serves people rather than pride.","symbolism":"A basalt throne gives weight to the ruler's responsibility; enduring stone asks whether authority protects what it holds.","aff":["I can be firm without closing my heart."],"question":"Which boundary would make your responsibilities more sustainable?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-emperor.webp","alt":"The Emperor: A basalt throne gives weight to the ruler's responsibility; enduring stone asks whether authority protects what it holds.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-hierophant","n":5,"rn":"V","name":"The Hierophant","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["tradition","learning","belonging"],"up":"A trusted practice, teacher, or community can offer a steady path. Learn its purpose as well as its form, then decide how to carry it.","rev":"Inherited rules deserve examination when they silence lived experience. Keep the wisdom that helps and question the authority that refuses reflection.","symbolism":"Silver keys in the Gothic sanctuary represent access to shared knowledge and the responsibility of those who keep it.","aff":["I can learn deeply and still ask why."],"question":"Which tradition supports you, and which needs a new question?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-hierophant.webp","alt":"The Hierophant: Silver keys in the Gothic sanctuary represent access to shared knowledge and the responsibility of those who keep it.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-lovers","n":6,"rn":"VI","name":"The Lovers","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["alignment","choice","relationship"],"up":"Choose in a way that brings your values and actions into relationship. Honest conversation can deepen a bond without erasing either person.","rev":"A divided commitment or unspoken need may be creating distance. Name what you value before deciding what agreement you can offer.","symbolism":"The rose gate holds two figures in one threshold, inviting connection that honors both closeness and individual choice.","aff":["I choose connection with integrity."],"question":"Where could a more honest choice bring your life into alignment?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-lovers.webp","alt":"The Lovers: The rose gate holds two figures in one threshold, inviting connection that honors both closeness and individual choice.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-chariot","n":7,"rn":"VII","name":"The Chariot","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["direction","resolve","discipline"],"up":"Give opposing impulses a shared destination. Progress comes from purposeful steering and consistent effort rather than force alone.","rev":"If momentum has become haste, slow down and check who is holding the reins. A clearer direction matters more than a faster pace.","symbolism":"The cathedral gateway frames a departure; the chariot gathers contrasting forces into a single, chosen movement.","aff":["I guide my energy toward what matters."],"question":"What destination could organize your competing demands?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-chariot.webp","alt":"The Chariot: The cathedral gateway frames a departure; the chariot gathers contrasting forces into a single, chosen movement.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"strength","n":8,"rn":"VIII","name":"Strength","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["courage","compassion","patience"],"up":"Meet intensity with a steady presence. Gentle persistence can transform a difficult encounter more deeply than domination.","rev":"Exhaustion or self-criticism may be wearing the mask of discipline. Rest, ask for help, and practice the kindness you would offer another.","symbolism":"The rose chapel joins vulnerability with courage, and the animal companion gives instinct a place within conscious care.","aff":["My gentleness has strength."],"question":"What would courage look like if it did not require harshness?","image":"/cards/gothic/strength.webp","alt":"Strength: The rose chapel joins vulnerability with courage, and the animal companion gives instinct a place within conscious care.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-hermit","n":9,"rn":"IX","name":"The Hermit","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["solitude","discernment","guidance"],"up":"Step away from the chorus long enough to hear your own thinking. A modest light can reveal the next step without illuminating the entire road.","rev":"Solitude may be turning into isolation, or constant company may be preventing reflection. Seek a rhythm of retreat and return.","symbolism":"The star lantern illuminates a small circle in the cathedral's shadow, making inner guidance useful one step at a time.","aff":["A quiet light is enough for the next step."],"question":"What becomes clearer when you give yourself unhurried time?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-hermit.webp","alt":"The Hermit: The star lantern illuminates a small circle in the cathedral's shadow, making inner guidance useful one step at a time.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"wheel-of-fortune","n":10,"rn":"X","name":"Wheel of Fortune","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["cycles","change","adaptability"],"up":"Circumstances are moving. Notice what is opening, accept what you cannot command, and use your choices where they have real influence.","rev":"Repeating patterns may need attention rather than another attempt to force timing. Look for the part of the cycle you can respond to differently.","symbolism":"The great cathedral wheel evokes seasons, chance, and the turning of experience beyond any single person's command.","aff":["I can respond wisely to a changing world."],"question":"Which part of this change is yours to shape?","image":"/cards/gothic/wheel-of-fortune.webp","alt":"Wheel of Fortune: The great cathedral wheel evokes seasons, chance, and the turning of experience beyond any single person's command.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"justice","n":11,"rn":"XI","name":"Justice","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["fairness","truth","accountability"],"up":"Look at the evidence and the consequences of your choices. A fair decision holds compassion and responsibility in the same clear light.","rev":"A missing perspective or double standard may be distorting judgment. Correct the record and allow accountability to include repair.","symbolism":"Silver scales balance beneath Gothic stone, pairing impartial attention with the human weight of every decision.","aff":["I seek truth with an open and accountable heart."],"question":"Whose perspective would make your next decision fairer?","image":"/cards/gothic/justice.webp","alt":"Justice: Silver scales balance beneath Gothic stone, pairing impartial attention with the human weight of every decision.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-hanged-man","n":12,"rn":"XII","name":"The Hanged Man","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["perspective","pause","surrender"],"up":"A willing pause can reveal a view effort could not reach. Let an old assumption loosen before deciding what comes next.","rev":"Waiting may have become a way to avoid a necessary choice. Distinguish a fruitful pause from a sacrifice that no longer serves you.","symbolism":"The suspended figure changes the chapel's ordinary orientation, making stillness an active experiment in perspective.","aff":["I allow a different view to emerge."],"question":"What might change if you stopped pushing for a moment?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-hanged-man.webp","alt":"The Hanged Man: The suspended figure changes the chapel's ordinary orientation, making stillness an active experiment in perspective.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"death","n":13,"rn":"XIII","name":"Death","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["transition","release","renewal"],"up":"An ending asks to be acknowledged. Release what has completed its purpose so that new life has actual room to take root.","rev":"Holding tightly to a finished chapter can prolong its ache. Make one gentle, concrete gesture of closure rather than demanding instant renewal.","symbolism":"The skeletal rider beneath the arch embodies the passage of seasons and identities, not a prediction of physical death.","aff":["I can honor an ending and welcome becoming."],"question":"What has ended in practice but not yet in your heart?","image":"/cards/gothic/death.webp","alt":"Death: The skeletal rider beneath the arch embodies the passage of seasons and identities, not a prediction of physical death.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"temperance","n":14,"rn":"XIV","name":"Temperance","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["balance","integration","healing"],"up":"Bring differences into conversation at a pace they can sustain. Small adjustments and repeated care create a workable harmony.","rev":"Too much of one ingredient may be overwhelming the whole. Simplify the mixture and restore a rhythm that includes rest.","symbolism":"Water exchanged beside the cloister pool makes balance visible as a living process of adjustment rather than a fixed ideal.","aff":["I grow through patient integration."],"question":"Which small adjustment would bring your day closer to balance?","image":"/cards/gothic/temperance.webp","alt":"Temperance: Water exchanged beside the cloister pool makes balance visible as a living process of adjustment rather than a fixed ideal.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-devil","n":15,"rn":"XV","name":"The Devil","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["attachment","awareness","liberation"],"up":"Look closely at the bargain that keeps you small. Naming a habit, temptation, or unequal arrangement can reveal where choice remains.","rev":"A binding pattern may be loosening, though shame can pull you back. Support freedom with practical boundaries and compassionate accountability.","symbolism":"Unlocked chains beneath the horned shadow show how fear can make an attachment feel more absolute than it is.","aff":["Awareness opens a space for choice."],"question":"What apparent obligation could you examine more freely?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-devil.webp","alt":"The Devil: Unlocked chains beneath the horned shadow show how fear can make an attachment feel more absolute than it is.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-tower","n":16,"rn":"XVI","name":"The Tower","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["disruption","revelation","rebuilding"],"up":"A structure can no longer hide its weakness. Attend to immediate needs, let the truth arrive, and rebuild around what can honestly support you.","rev":"An avoided problem may be gathering force, or the shock may already be passing. Seek support and address the foundation before restoring appearances.","symbolism":"The storm-struck tower and scattering ravens reveal the cost of false security and the possibility of a more truthful sky.","aff":["I can rebuild on honest ground."],"question":"Which truth would help you build something sounder?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-tower.webp","alt":"The Tower: The storm-struck tower and scattering ravens reveal the cost of false security and the possibility of a more truthful sky.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-star","n":17,"rn":"XVII","name":"The Star","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["hope","renewal","openness"],"up":"Let recovery be simple and sincere. A small act of care can restore trust in the future without requiring certainty.","rev":"Hope may feel distant after strain. Lower the demand for inspiration and begin with a tangible source of replenishment.","symbolism":"Starlight over the abbey offers orientation after darkness; the open night invites vulnerability without spectacle.","aff":["I make space for hope to return."],"question":"What modest source of renewal can you reach today?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-star.webp","alt":"The Star: Starlight over the abbey offers orientation after darkness; the open night invites vulnerability without spectacle.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-moon","n":18,"rn":"XVIII","name":"The Moon","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["uncertainty","imagination","instinct"],"up":"Travel carefully through partial light. Notice dreams and feelings, then check assumptions before turning them into conclusions.","rev":"Confusion may be clearing, or an unexamined fear may still be steering you. Separate what you know from what you imagine.","symbolism":"The cathedral path under the moon holds ambiguity, reminding the traveler that a compelling shadow is not always a reliable map.","aff":["I can hold uncertainty without inventing certainty."],"question":"Which fear needs evidence, and which feeling needs care?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-moon.webp","alt":"The Moon: The cathedral path under the moon holds ambiguity, reminding the traveler that a compelling shadow is not always a reliable map.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-sun","n":19,"rn":"XIX","name":"The Sun","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["joy","clarity","vitality"],"up":"Welcome the warmth that is available. Shared delight and straightforward expression can reconnect you with confidence and play.","rev":"Pressure to appear happy may be hiding a quieter need. Seek uncomplicated pleasure and allow joy to return at its own scale.","symbolism":"The bright courtyard and white pony bring life into the Gothic world, showing that darkness and delight can inhabit one story.","aff":["I allow myself to receive the light."],"question":"What would make room for a little unperformed joy?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-sun.webp","alt":"The Sun: The bright courtyard and white pony bring life into the Gothic world, showing that darkness and delight can inhabit one story.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"judgement","n":20,"rn":"XX","name":"Judgement","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["awakening","reckoning","calling"],"up":"Hear the invitation to live more honestly. Review the past with compassion, take responsibility, and answer the work that now calls you.","rev":"Harsh self-judgment or fear of change may be muffling the call. Learn from what happened without making it your permanent identity.","symbolism":"The silver herald above the roofless abbey opens the old sanctuary to the sky, joining remembrance with a new beginning.","aff":["I can answer the next chapter with honesty."],"question":"What lesson are you ready to turn into a changed action?","image":"/cards/gothic/judgement.webp","alt":"Judgement: The silver herald above the roofless abbey opens the old sanctuary to the sky, joining remembrance with a new beginning.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"the-world","n":21,"rn":"XXI","name":"The World","arcana":"Major","suit":null,"keywords":["completion","integration","belonging"],"up":"A meaningful cycle comes together. Recognize what you have learned, celebrate the work, and carry its gifts into the wider world.","rev":"A final loose thread or reluctance to finish may be delaying closure. Define what complete means and honor that boundary.","symbolism":"The Gothic rose window gathers many forms into one whole, allowing difference to remain visible within belonging.","aff":["I honor the wholeness of this journey."],"question":"What deserves acknowledgment before you begin again?","image":"/cards/gothic/the-world.webp","alt":"The World: The Gothic rose window gathers many forms into one whole, allowing difference to remain visible within belonging.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"ace-of-wands","n":22,"rn":"Ace","name":"Ace of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["inspiration","spark","potential"],"up":"A creative impulse is asking for an experiment. Give the spark one small action while its energy is fresh.","rev":"A delayed beginning or restless idea may need a clearer purpose. Restore interest before demanding momentum.","symbolism":"The single living wand carries fire into the cathedral's cool stone, making potential visible before a plan exists.","aff":["I give one promising spark a place to grow."],"question":"Which idea is ready for a small real experiment?","image":"/cards/gothic/ace-of-wands.webp","alt":"Ace of Wands: The single living wand carries fire into the cathedral's cool stone, making potential visible before a plan exists.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"two-of-wands","n":23,"rn":"Two","name":"Two of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["planning","vision","choice"],"up":"Survey the possibilities beyond your familiar walls. Choose a direction that fits your deeper intention and prepare to leave the overlook.","rev":"Endless comparison may be postponing a workable choice. Gather the missing information and set a decision point.","symbolism":"Two wands frame a view beyond the cloister, making planning a bridge between shelter and departure.","aff":["I can choose a direction without seeing every mile."],"question":"What information would turn imagining into a decision?","image":"/cards/gothic/two-of-wands.webp","alt":"Two of Wands: Two wands frame a view beyond the cloister, making planning a bridge between shelter and departure.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"three-of-wands","n":24,"rn":"Three","name":"Three of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["expansion","foresight","enterprise"],"up":"Your effort is beginning to reach beyond its starting place. Look ahead, welcome collaboration, and prepare for a wider horizon.","rev":"Delays or limited support may be testing your expectations. Adjust the plan while keeping its purpose in view.","symbolism":"Three wands stand at the edge of the Gothic world, marking the moment when a private vision meets the distance.","aff":["I prepare to meet a wider world."],"question":"What support will you need when this work grows?","image":"/cards/gothic/three-of-wands.webp","alt":"Three of Wands: Three wands stand at the edge of the Gothic world, marking the moment when a private vision meets the distance.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"four-of-wands","n":25,"rn":"Four","name":"Four of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["celebration","home","community"],"up":"Pause to celebrate a foundation built together. A shared ritual or welcome can turn achievement into belonging.","rev":"A gathering may feel strained, or a private milestone may lack recognition. Create a form of celebration that fits your actual needs.","symbolism":"Four wands make a ceremonial threshold where old stone becomes a place of welcome.","aff":["I make room to celebrate what sustains me."],"question":"Which small milestone deserves shared recognition?","image":"/cards/gothic/four-of-wands.webp","alt":"Four of Wands: Four wands make a ceremonial threshold where old stone becomes a place of welcome.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"five-of-wands","n":26,"rn":"Five","name":"Five of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["friction","practice","competition"],"up":"Different energies are meeting without an agreed shape. Clarify the purpose of the contest and let disagreement sharpen rather than injure.","rev":"Avoided tension or constant rivalry may be using up the energy needed for the work. Name the conflict and agree on fair terms.","symbolism":"Crossing wands turn the cathedral court into a rehearsal for strength, skill, and learning to share space.","aff":["I can disagree without losing my center."],"question":"What agreement would make this friction useful?","image":"/cards/gothic/five-of-wands.webp","alt":"Five of Wands: Crossing wands turn the cathedral court into a rehearsal for strength, skill, and learning to share space.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"six-of-wands","n":27,"rn":"Six","name":"Six of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["recognition","confidence","progress"],"up":"Let your effort be seen and acknowledge those who helped it succeed. Recognition becomes steadier when it serves the work rather than replacing it.","rev":"External approval may be absent or carrying too much power. Measure progress by honest standards and share credit generously.","symbolism":"The ceremonial procession gives public form to achievement while the cathedral reminds the victor of a larger community.","aff":["I can receive recognition with gratitude."],"question":"How could you acknowledge progress without needing applause?","image":"/cards/gothic/six-of-wands.webp","alt":"Six of Wands: The ceremonial procession gives public form to achievement while the cathedral reminds the victor of a larger community.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"seven-of-wands","n":28,"rn":"Seven","name":"Seven of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["conviction","boundaries","courage"],"up":"Stand for what you have chosen with a clear sense of purpose. A firm boundary can protect your work without turning every encounter into a battle.","rev":"Defensiveness or too many demands may be draining your resolve. Choose which ground is truly worth holding.","symbolism":"Raised wands and an elevated position evoke the pressure of defending a hard-won place.","aff":["I choose the ground I am willing to protect."],"question":"Which boundary serves your values, and which protects only pride?","image":"/cards/gothic/seven-of-wands.webp","alt":"Seven of Wands: Raised wands and an elevated position evoke the pressure of defending a hard-won place.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"eight-of-wands","n":29,"rn":"Eight","name":"Eight of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["movement","communication","timing"],"up":"Events or messages are moving quickly. Respond clearly, coordinate with others, and use the opening while keeping attention on direction.","rev":"Haste, mixed signals, or delay may be scattering momentum. Verify the message before sending more energy after it.","symbolism":"The flight of eight wands cuts through the still Gothic sky, making speed and trajectory the central symbols.","aff":["I move with clarity as well as energy."],"question":"What needs a clear response before momentum carries it further?","image":"/cards/gothic/eight-of-wands.webp","alt":"Eight of Wands: The flight of eight wands cuts through the still Gothic sky, making speed and trajectory the central symbols.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"nine-of-wands","n":30,"rn":"Nine","name":"Nine of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["resilience","vigilance","recovery"],"up":"Your experience has taught you endurance. Protect what matters while making enough room for rest and appropriate help.","rev":"Constant watchfulness may be outliving the danger. Examine which defenses still protect you and which prevent recovery.","symbolism":"The guarded line of wands holds the history of effort, asking the watcher to balance readiness with repair.","aff":["I can protect my work and still accept rest."],"question":"Where could you lower your guard safely enough to recover?","image":"/cards/gothic/nine-of-wands.webp","alt":"Nine of Wands: The guarded line of wands holds the history of effort, asking the watcher to balance readiness with repair.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"ten-of-wands","n":31,"rn":"Ten","name":"Ten of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["burden","limits","responsibility"],"up":"A worthwhile effort has become heavy. Sort what is yours to carry, share the load, and make the finish sustainable.","rev":"An unsustainable burden may be ready to be set down. Ask for specific help instead of waiting for others to guess.","symbolism":"The gathered wands become a weight that obscures the path, showing how duty can crowd out direction.","aff":["Responsibility can include asking for help."],"question":"Which task could be shared, simplified, or released?","image":"/cards/gothic/ten-of-wands.webp","alt":"Ten of Wands: The gathered wands become a weight that obscures the path, showing how duty can crowd out direction.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"page-of-wands","n":32,"rn":"Page","name":"Page of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["curiosity","discovery","enthusiasm"],"up":"Approach the unfamiliar as a learner. Let playful exploration reveal a creative path before you demand mastery.","rev":"A promising impulse may be distracted by novelty or afraid of looking inexperienced. Pick one practice and give it patient attention.","symbolism":"The young wanderer studies a living wand as an invitation to discover what the world might become.","aff":["I let curiosity teach me where to begin."],"question":"What would you try if being a beginner felt welcome?","image":"/cards/gothic/page-of-wands.webp","alt":"Page of Wands: The young wanderer studies a living wand as an invitation to discover what the world might become.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"knight-of-wands","n":33,"rn":"Knight","name":"Knight of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["adventure","boldness","momentum"],"up":"Bring courage to a meaningful pursuit. Enthusiasm is most useful when paired with enough follow-through to carry the work home.","rev":"Impatience or changing direction too often may leave others carrying the consequences. Slow the charge and make a sustainable promise.","symbolism":"The moving rider carries the suit's fire out of the sanctuary and into uncertain country.","aff":["I give my boldness a direction it can sustain."],"question":"What commitment would help your enthusiasm last?","image":"/cards/gothic/knight-of-wands.webp","alt":"Knight of Wands: The moving rider carries the suit's fire out of the sanctuary and into uncertain country.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"queen-of-wands","n":34,"rn":"Queen","name":"Queen of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["warmth","self-trust","magnetism"],"up":"Lead with a warmth that leaves others room to shine. Confidence grows when your creative life and your boundaries support each other.","rev":"Comparison or overextension may be dimming your presence. Return to what delights you and protect the energy it needs.","symbolism":"The sovereign of living fire holds a confident place in the Gothic court, joining creative power with animal instinct.","aff":["I can be fully present without shrinking another."],"question":"What helps your confidence feel generous rather than guarded?","image":"/cards/gothic/queen-of-wands.webp","alt":"Queen of Wands: The sovereign of living fire holds a confident place in the Gothic court, joining creative power with animal instinct.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"king-of-wands","n":35,"rn":"King","name":"King of Wands","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Wands","keywords":["vision","leadership","enterprise"],"up":"Give a shared vision a clear direction. Invite capable people into the work and hold responsibility for the climate you create.","rev":"A strong vision may be turning rigid or neglecting details. Listen to dissent and bring your promises into accountable practice.","symbolism":"The fire sovereign's throne gives ambition a seat of responsibility within the cathedral world.","aff":["I guide a vision with courage and accountability."],"question":"Who needs to be heard before you lead the next step?","image":"/cards/gothic/king-of-wands.webp","alt":"King of Wands: The fire sovereign's throne gives ambition a seat of responsibility within the cathedral world.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"ace-of-cups","n":36,"rn":"Ace","name":"Ace of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["openness","feeling","renewal"],"up":"Let a fresh feeling arrive without immediately defining its future. A small gesture of kindness can begin a new emotional season.","rev":"An empty cup or guarded heart may need attention before it can offer more. Receive care and allow feeling its own pace.","symbolism":"The solitary cup offers water within the stone sanctuary, a living source in a place of quiet reflection.","aff":["I make space to receive what is gentle."],"question":"What feeling could you welcome without needing to explain it?","image":"/cards/gothic/ace-of-cups.webp","alt":"Ace of Cups: The solitary cup offers water within the stone sanctuary, a living source in a place of quiet reflection.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"two-of-cups","n":37,"rn":"Two","name":"Two of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["mutuality","partnership","trust"],"up":"Meet another person in honest exchange. Reciprocity grows through listening, consent, and a willingness to be changed by the encounter.","rev":"An imbalance or unspoken expectation may be weakening trust. Name what each person can genuinely offer.","symbolism":"Two cups create a shared center while leaving each vessel distinct, honoring connection without loss of self.","aff":["I welcome relationships that have room for both of us."],"question":"What would a more reciprocal exchange look like?","image":"/cards/gothic/two-of-cups.webp","alt":"Two of Cups: Two cups create a shared center while leaving each vessel distinct, honoring connection without loss of self.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"three-of-cups","n":38,"rn":"Three","name":"Three of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["friendship","celebration","support"],"up":"Joy becomes richer when it is shared. Let trusted companions celebrate with you and offer the kind of belonging you can also give.","rev":"Social strain, exclusion, or too many obligations may be obscuring real friendship. Seek a smaller, more nourishing circle.","symbolism":"Three cups form a gathering within the Gothic world, making companionship a shelter rather than a performance.","aff":["I let friendship be a source of nourishment."],"question":"Who could share a small joy or honest conversation with you?","image":"/cards/gothic/three-of-cups.webp","alt":"Three of Cups: Three cups form a gathering within the Gothic world, making companionship a shelter rather than a performance.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"four-of-cups","n":39,"rn":"Four","name":"Four of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["contemplation","apathy","receptivity"],"up":"A pause may be asking you to understand what no longer nourishes. Look at the available offer without forcing yourself to want it.","rev":"Interest may be returning after withdrawal, or avoidance may still be disguising itself as reflection. Test one gentle re-engagement.","symbolism":"The still arrangement of cups holds both emotional weariness and the possibility of an unnoticed invitation.","aff":["I can pause and remain open to a new invitation."],"question":"What offer have you dismissed before understanding it?","image":"/cards/gothic/four-of-cups.webp","alt":"Four of Cups: The still arrangement of cups holds both emotional weariness and the possibility of an unnoticed invitation.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"five-of-cups","n":40,"rn":"Five","name":"Five of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["grief","perspective","remaining-gifts"],"up":"Let disappointment have its truthful weight. When you are ready, notice what remains and who can accompany you through the loss.","rev":"Recovery may be beginning, though loyalty to sorrow can make relief feel disloyal. Let memory and renewed connection coexist.","symbolism":"Fallen and standing cups share the same scene, giving loss and continuing possibility equal reality.","aff":["I honor what is lost and what remains."],"question":"What still supports you beside this disappointment?","image":"/cards/gothic/five-of-cups.webp","alt":"Five of Cups: Fallen and standing cups share the same scene, giving loss and continuing possibility equal reality.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"six-of-cups","n":41,"rn":"Six","name":"Six of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["memory","tenderness","roots"],"up":"A memory or familiar kindness may reconnect you with something simple and true. Receive its gift while remaining present to who you are now.","rev":"Nostalgia may be smoothing away important truths or keeping you in an old role. Keep the tenderness and update the story.","symbolism":"The cups carry the gentleness of an earlier season into the cathedral's weathered space.","aff":["I can carry kindness forward without living in the past."],"question":"Which remembered kindness could you offer in a new form?","image":"/cards/gothic/six-of-cups.webp","alt":"Six of Cups: The cups carry the gentleness of an earlier season into the cathedral's weathered space.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"seven-of-cups","n":42,"rn":"Seven","name":"Seven of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["imagination","options","discernment"],"up":"Several possibilities are calling at once. Enjoy imagining, then look closely at what each option asks of your real life.","rev":"Overwhelm or a seductive fantasy may be clearing. Choose one possibility to investigate rather than treating every image as a promise.","symbolism":"The many cups hold differing visions, turning desire into a gallery that requires discernment.","aff":["I can dream freely and choose carefully."],"question":"Which possibility deserves facts before it earns commitment?","image":"/cards/gothic/seven-of-cups.webp","alt":"Seven of Cups: The many cups hold differing visions, turning desire into a gallery that requires discernment.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"eight-of-cups","n":43,"rn":"Eight","name":"Eight of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["departure","search","emotional-truth"],"up":"Walk away from what no longer answers your deeper need. A respectful departure can honor the past without asking it to become your future.","rev":"Fear of leaving or habitual withdrawal may be clouding the choice. Clarify whether you need a new agreement or a genuine goodbye.","symbolism":"The moonlit passage beyond the cups embodies a search for meaning that possessions or appearances cannot complete.","aff":["I may seek what is missing without denying what was good."],"question":"What need would you be walking toward rather than merely away from?","image":"/cards/gothic/eight-of-cups.webp","alt":"Eight of Cups: The moonlit passage beyond the cups embodies a search for meaning that possessions or appearances cannot complete.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"nine-of-cups","n":44,"rn":"Nine","name":"Nine of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["contentment","gratitude","pleasure"],"up":"Enjoy a wish or comfort that has taken real shape. Gratitude becomes fuller when you let yourself experience satisfaction without hoarding it.","rev":"A polished picture of success may be hiding an unmet need. Ask which pleasures nourish you and which only distract.","symbolism":"The gathered cups create a chamber of plenty, inviting reflection on what makes abundance satisfying.","aff":["I can savor enough."],"question":"What is already good enough to enjoy without improving it?","image":"/cards/gothic/nine-of-cups.webp","alt":"Nine of Cups: The gathered cups create a chamber of plenty, inviting reflection on what makes abundance satisfying.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"ten-of-cups","n":45,"rn":"Ten","name":"Ten of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["belonging","harmony","shared-life"],"up":"A sense of emotional home can grow through repeated acts of care. Celebrate connection while keeping room for each person's difference.","rev":"An ideal of harmony may be making honest needs difficult to name. Repair begins with a truthful conversation, not a perfect picture.","symbolism":"The completed arc of cups links individual feeling to a wider life of shared shelter and care.","aff":["I help create belonging through everyday care."],"question":"What ordinary act would make your shared life kinder?","image":"/cards/gothic/ten-of-cups.webp","alt":"Ten of Cups: The completed arc of cups links individual feeling to a wider life of shared shelter and care.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"page-of-cups","n":46,"rn":"Page","name":"Page of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["sensitivity","imagination","surprise"],"up":"An unexpected feeling or creative message deserves a curious welcome. Stay receptive without surrendering your judgment.","rev":"Shyness, unrealistic expectations, or fear of embarrassment may be blocking expression. Offer a small honest message rather than a flawless one.","symbolism":"The young cup bearer listens for a surprising voice within the vessel, giving imagination a playful form.","aff":["I can meet my feelings with curiosity."],"question":"What small emotional truth could you express gently?","image":"/cards/gothic/page-of-cups.webp","alt":"Page of Cups: The young cup bearer listens for a surprising voice within the vessel, giving imagination a playful form.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"knight-of-cups","n":47,"rn":"Knight","name":"Knight of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["romance","idealism","invitation"],"up":"Carry an invitation with sincerity. Let imagination make life richer while allowing actions to show the depth of your care.","rev":"A beautiful promise may be outrunning reliability. Look for the practical gesture that can support the feeling.","symbolism":"The cup-bearing rider moves through the Gothic landscape as a messenger of feeling and possibility.","aff":["I let my actions carry my heartfelt intentions."],"question":"How could you make a hopeful feeling tangible?","image":"/cards/gothic/knight-of-cups.webp","alt":"Knight of Cups: The cup-bearing rider moves through the Gothic landscape as a messenger of feeling and possibility.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"queen-of-cups","n":48,"rn":"Queen","name":"Queen of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["empathy","intuition","care"],"up":"Listen deeply while staying rooted in your own emotional life. Compassion can hold another's feeling without taking ownership of it.","rev":"Absorbing others' needs or withholding your own may be exhausting you. Restore a boundary that makes real care possible.","symbolism":"The queen's attentive relationship with the cup gives feeling a place of dignity and reflective depth.","aff":["My care includes my own inner life."],"question":"Where would a compassionate boundary help you listen more freely?","image":"/cards/gothic/queen-of-cups.webp","alt":"Queen of Cups: The queen's attentive relationship with the cup gives feeling a place of dignity and reflective depth.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"king-of-cups","n":49,"rn":"King","name":"King of Cups","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Cups","keywords":["composure","maturity","compassion"],"up":"Bring emotional steadiness to a changing situation. You can acknowledge difficult feelings and still choose a measured, caring response.","rev":"Suppression or indirect control may be replacing honest emotional leadership. Name the feeling and choose a response you can stand behind.","symbolism":"The cup sovereign remains centered amid the suit's waters, embodying feeling held with judgment rather than denied.","aff":["I can feel deeply and respond with care."],"question":"What response would honor both your feelings and your responsibilities?","image":"/cards/gothic/king-of-cups.webp","alt":"King of Cups: The cup sovereign remains centered amid the suit's waters, embodying feeling held with judgment rather than denied.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"ace-of-swords","n":50,"rn":"Ace","name":"Ace of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["clarity","truth","decision"],"up":"A clear insight cuts through a tangled question. State what you know plainly and use that understanding with care.","rev":"Conflicting information or forceful language may be obscuring the issue. Check assumptions before making a sharp conclusion.","symbolism":"The single silver blade brings a line of clarity into the cathedral's shadows.","aff":["I use clarity to understand rather than wound."],"question":"Which fact would make the next decision clearer?","image":"/cards/gothic/ace-of-swords.webp","alt":"Ace of Swords: The single silver blade brings a line of clarity into the cathedral's shadows.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"two-of-swords","n":51,"rn":"Two","name":"Two of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["stalemate","discernment","choice"],"up":"A difficult choice may need protected thinking time. Identify what you are refusing to see as well as what remains unknown.","rev":"Avoidance or information overload may be making balance impossible. Let one relevant truth begin to move the decision.","symbolism":"The paired swords hold tension in stillness, asking whether equilibrium is wisdom or delay.","aff":["I can face a choice one truth at a time."],"question":"What are you protecting yourself from knowing?","image":"/cards/gothic/two-of-swords.webp","alt":"Two of Swords: The paired swords hold tension in stillness, asking whether equilibrium is wisdom or delay.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"three-of-swords","n":52,"rn":"Three","name":"Three of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["heartache","honesty","repair"],"up":"A painful truth needs room to be felt. Kindness and clear language can begin repair even when they cannot undo what happened.","rev":"Sorrow may be loosening, or resentment may be keeping the wound open. Seek a form of expression that allows care to reach it.","symbolism":"Three blades give emotional pain a visible shape within the Gothic sanctuary, making acknowledgment possible.","aff":["I can meet pain with tenderness and truth."],"question":"What would help you express the hurt without deepening it?","image":"/cards/gothic/three-of-swords.webp","alt":"Three of Swords: Three blades give emotional pain a visible shape within the Gothic sanctuary, making acknowledgment possible.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"four-of-swords","n":53,"rn":"Four","name":"Four of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["rest","retreat","integration"],"up":"Step back from the struggle long enough to recover perspective. Protected rest is part of the work, not a reward for finishing everything.","rev":"Restlessness or depletion may be asking for a different pace. Return gradually and protect the recovery you have begun.","symbolism":"The quiet chapel and resting swords make a sanctuary from constant reaction.","aff":["I give my mind permission to rest."],"question":"What can remain unanswered while you recover?","image":"/cards/gothic/four-of-swords.webp","alt":"Four of Swords: The quiet chapel and resting swords make a sanctuary from constant reaction.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"five-of-swords","n":54,"rn":"Five","name":"Five of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["conflict","cost","repair"],"up":"Ask what winning would cost here. A boundary, a departure, or an honest repair may serve you better than a final argument.","rev":"A conflict may be ready for reconciliation, but agreement needs accountability. Notice whether the underlying pattern has changed.","symbolism":"The aftermath of the sword contest makes the human cost of victory visible.","aff":["I can choose dignity over an empty victory."],"question":"Which outcome matters more than having the last word?","image":"/cards/gothic/five-of-swords.webp","alt":"Five of Swords: The aftermath of the sword contest makes the human cost of victory visible.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"six-of-swords","n":55,"rn":"Six","name":"Six of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["transition","perspective","passage"],"up":"Move toward calmer conditions with the knowledge your experience has given you. You need not feel resolved to begin a useful passage.","rev":"An unfinished concern may be making the crossing harder. Seek practical support and distinguish necessary baggage from familiar weight.","symbolism":"The journey with six swords carries memory across the water rather than leaving all experience behind.","aff":["I can move toward greater steadiness."],"question":"What would make the next transition easier to navigate?","image":"/cards/gothic/six-of-swords.webp","alt":"Six of Swords: The journey with six swords carries memory across the water rather than leaving all experience behind.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"seven-of-swords","n":56,"rn":"Seven","name":"Seven of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["strategy","secrecy","discernment"],"up":"Choose your approach thoughtfully and protect appropriate privacy. Make sure strategy remains consistent with the trust you want to keep.","rev":"A hidden motive or evasive tactic may be ready to come into the open. Correct course before a clever shortcut becomes a costly pattern.","symbolism":"The cautious figure and watchful fox evoke intelligence, concealment, and the line between discretion and deception.","aff":["I can be resourceful without betraying my values."],"question":"Where is privacy useful, and where is honesty overdue?","image":"/cards/gothic/seven-of-swords.webp","alt":"Seven of Swords: The cautious figure and watchful fox evoke intelligence, concealment, and the line between discretion and deception.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"eight-of-swords","n":57,"rn":"Eight","name":"Eight of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["restriction","beliefs","agency"],"up":"A situation may feel narrower than it is. Identify one real constraint and one assumption, then look for a supported next move.","rev":"A limiting story may be loosening its hold. Practice the freedom in a small action and recognize where support is still needed.","symbolism":"The circle of swords frames an apparent enclosure, inviting examination of both actual barriers and fearful interpretation.","aff":["I look for the choice that remains available."],"question":"Which limit is a fact, and which could be tested?","image":"/cards/gothic/eight-of-swords.webp","alt":"Eight of Swords: The circle of swords frames an apparent enclosure, inviting examination of both actual barriers and fearful interpretation.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"nine-of-swords","n":58,"rn":"Nine","name":"Nine of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["worry","vulnerability","perspective"],"up":"Anxious thoughts are asking for care, not unquestioned belief. Bring the concern into daylight through rest, evidence, or a trusted conversation.","rev":"Distress may be easing, or you may be hiding how much you carry. Let support reach the real concern rather than the polished explanation.","symbolism":"The night chamber and suspended blades give sleepless worry a symbolic architecture.","aff":["I do not have to face every worry alone."],"question":"What would help you distinguish a problem from a feared possibility?","image":"/cards/gothic/nine-of-swords.webp","alt":"Nine of Swords: The night chamber and suspended blades give sleepless worry a symbolic architecture.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"ten-of-swords","n":59,"rn":"Ten","name":"Ten of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["ending","exhaustion","recovery"],"up":"A painful pattern has reached its limit. Stop asking the exhausted chapter to provide the next answer and begin with immediate care.","rev":"The worst may be passing, though fear can keep you braced for another blow. Accept gradual recovery and avoid reopening what is complete.","symbolism":"The ten swords make finality visible while the returning light suggests that an ending is not the whole horizon.","aff":["I may begin recovery without solving the whole future."],"question":"What does the first kind step after this ending look like?","image":"/cards/gothic/ten-of-swords.webp","alt":"Ten of Swords: The ten swords make finality visible while the returning light suggests that an ending is not the whole horizon.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"page-of-swords","n":60,"rn":"Page","name":"Page of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["inquiry","alertness","learning"],"up":"Ask a precise question and follow the evidence with curiosity. Careful observation is more useful than a quick display of certainty.","rev":"Rumor, defensiveness, or constant monitoring may be clouding attention. Verify what you repeat and let curiosity soften your stance.","symbolism":"The young sword bearer watches the changing air, representing a mind learning how to use its edge.","aff":["I can ask clearly and remain open to learning."],"question":"Which assumption deserves a sincere question?","image":"/cards/gothic/page-of-swords.webp","alt":"Page of Swords: The young sword bearer watches the changing air, representing a mind learning how to use its edge.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"knight-of-swords","n":61,"rn":"Knight","name":"Knight of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["conviction","urgency","directness"],"up":"Bring decisive effort to an issue that needs movement. Keep your purpose clear enough to notice the people and facts along the way.","rev":"Speed or certainty may be carrying you past essential context. Slow the argument long enough to listen.","symbolism":"The charging sword rider embodies the force of an idea turned rapidly into action.","aff":["I give my conviction the discipline of attention."],"question":"What would you understand better if you slowed down before acting?","image":"/cards/gothic/knight-of-swords.webp","alt":"Knight of Swords: The charging sword rider embodies the force of an idea turned rapidly into action.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"queen-of-swords","n":62,"rn":"Queen","name":"Queen of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["discernment","independence","candor"],"up":"Speak with clarity shaped by experience. An honest boundary can be humane, and compassion need not make your judgment vague.","rev":"Sharpness or guardedness may be protecting an old hurt. Keep the truth while choosing a form that leaves room for understanding.","symbolism":"The queen's silver blade and watchful presence join clear judgment with the knowledge of lived difficulty.","aff":["I can be clear and compassionate together."],"question":"How could you say the truth without making another person smaller?","image":"/cards/gothic/queen-of-swords.webp","alt":"Queen of Swords: The queen's silver blade and watchful presence join clear judgment with the knowledge of lived difficulty.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"king-of-swords","n":63,"rn":"King","name":"King of Swords","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Swords","keywords":["reason","ethics","authority"],"up":"Use reason to create a fair and understandable decision. Share your standards and remain accountable to the people affected.","rev":"Rigid logic or persuasive language may be hiding a biased premise. Revisit the evidence and invite informed challenge.","symbolism":"The sword sovereign's seat embodies intellectual authority and the ethical burden of using it.","aff":["My judgment stays open to evidence and responsibility."],"question":"What principle should remain consistent in this decision?","image":"/cards/gothic/king-of-swords.webp","alt":"King of Swords: The sword sovereign's seat embodies intellectual authority and the ethical burden of using it.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"ace-of-pentacles","n":64,"rn":"Ace","name":"Ace of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["opportunity","grounding","resources"],"up":"A practical opportunity can become something lasting through patient care. Begin with a tangible step and a realistic sense of resources.","rev":"A promising opening may need more preparation or a clearer commitment. Check the foundation before investing further.","symbolism":"The golden pentacle above a stone hand brings possibility into the material world: time, shelter, work, and care.","aff":["I give possibility a practical beginning."],"question":"What small investment would help this opportunity take root?","image":"/cards/gothic/ace-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Ace of Pentacles: The golden pentacle above a stone hand brings possibility into the material world: time, shelter, work, and care.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"two-of-pentacles","n":65,"rn":"Two","name":"Two of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["adaptability","priorities","rhythm"],"up":"Balance changing demands through deliberate adjustments. Protect your essentials and let the plan move rather than demanding a perfect equilibrium.","rev":"Too many competing obligations may be overwhelming the rhythm. Choose what matters most and make the tradeoff explicit.","symbolism":"Two gold pentacles held in motion show balance as a practiced rhythm rather than a motionless state.","aff":["I can adjust without abandoning what matters."],"question":"Which priority needs a clearer place in your week?","image":"/cards/gothic/two-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Two of Pentacles: Two gold pentacles held in motion show balance as a practiced rhythm rather than a motionless state.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"three-of-pentacles","n":66,"rn":"Three","name":"Three of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["craft","collaboration","learning"],"up":"Good work grows when different skills meet with respect. Share the plan, invite feedback, and let each contribution be visible.","rev":"Unclear roles or unrecognized effort may be undermining the work. Agree on standards and make room to learn from one another.","symbolism":"The cathedral's three pentacles honor the craft and cooperation required to raise something larger than one person's effort.","aff":["I contribute my skill and welcome the skill of others."],"question":"What conversation would improve the way you work together?","image":"/cards/gothic/three-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Three of Pentacles: The cathedral's three pentacles honor the craft and cooperation required to raise something larger than one person's effort.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"four-of-pentacles","n":67,"rn":"Four","name":"Four of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["security","stewardship","control"],"up":"Protect what you have built while asking what enough means. Good stewardship keeps resources useful rather than merely locked away.","rev":"Fear of scarcity or careless release may be directing your choices. Find a boundary between hoarding and overgiving.","symbolism":"Four pentacles create a guarded enclosure around the figure, making security and restriction visible together.","aff":["I can care for my resources without closing my life."],"question":"What would help security feel steady rather than fearful?","image":"/cards/gothic/four-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Four of Pentacles: Four pentacles create a guarded enclosure around the figure, making security and restriction visible together.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"five-of-pentacles","n":68,"rn":"Five","name":"Five of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["hardship","solidarity","support"],"up":"A difficult material season deserves practical help and human dignity. Look for an accessible source of support and allow others to know what is needed.","rev":"Support or recovery may be within reach, though isolation can make it hard to receive. Take one concrete step toward assistance.","symbolism":"The cold cathedral threshold and illuminated pentacles hold need beside the possibility of shelter.","aff":["I deserve support during a difficult season."],"question":"What specific form of help would make the greatest difference now?","image":"/cards/gothic/five-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Five of Pentacles: The cold cathedral threshold and illuminated pentacles hold need beside the possibility of shelter.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"six-of-pentacles","n":69,"rn":"Six","name":"Six of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["generosity","reciprocity","fairness"],"up":"Give or receive with attention to dignity and context. A fair exchange considers power as well as the amount changing hands.","rev":"Conditional generosity or an unequal exchange may be creating dependence. Clarify terms and respect the recipient's agency.","symbolism":"The distribution of pentacles makes material exchange visible as an ethical relationship.","aff":["I let generosity preserve dignity."],"question":"What would make this exchange fairer for everyone involved?","image":"/cards/gothic/six-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Six of Pentacles: The distribution of pentacles makes material exchange visible as an ethical relationship.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"seven-of-pentacles","n":70,"rn":"Seven","name":"Seven of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["patience","assessment","cultivation"],"up":"Review what your steady effort is producing. Some growth needs more time; some needs a changed method or a wiser use of energy.","rev":"Impatience or sunk effort may be obscuring the evidence. Assess results honestly before committing another season.","symbolism":"Pentacles growing among tended vines link practical reward with seasons, care, and the uncertainty of cultivation.","aff":["I can be patient and still evaluate honestly."],"question":"What evidence would tell you whether to persist or adjust?","image":"/cards/gothic/seven-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Seven of Pentacles: Pentacles growing among tended vines link practical reward with seasons, care, and the uncertainty of cultivation.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"eight-of-pentacles","n":71,"rn":"Eight","name":"Eight of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["practice","skill","devotion"],"up":"Give repeated attention to a skill that matters. Improvement comes from useful feedback and the care you bring to ordinary work.","rev":"Perfectionism or repetition without learning may be limiting progress. Revisit the purpose and practice the part that actually needs attention.","symbolism":"The craftsperson's worked pentacles make learning visible through successive acts of care.","aff":["My craft grows through attentive practice."],"question":"Which small part of the work deserves deliberate practice?","image":"/cards/gothic/eight-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Eight of Pentacles: The craftsperson's worked pentacles make learning visible through successive acts of care.","artStatus":"finished"},{"id":"nine-of-pentacles","n":72,"rn":"Nine","name":"Nine of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["independence","refinement","sufficiency"],"up":"Enjoy the steadiness your effort has helped create. Independence can include receiving company and sharing abundance by choice.","rev":"A polished life may conceal isolation or overwork. Let comfort serve your wellbeing rather than become another standard to maintain.","symbolism":"The garden and watchful bird surround the pentacles with cultivated beauty, linking sufficiency to care and discernment.","aff":["I can enjoy what I have nurtured."],"question":"How could you experience the fruits of your work more fully?","image":"/cards/gothic/nine-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Nine of Pentacles: The garden and watchful bird surround the pentacles with cultivated beauty, linking sufficiency to care and discernment.","artStatus":"pending"},{"id":"ten-of-pentacles","n":73,"rn":"Ten","name":"Ten of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["legacy","continuity","shared-resources"],"up":"Consider the long life of your choices. A durable legacy includes knowledge, care, and fair access to what a household or community builds.","rev":"Inherited expectations or unequal access may need examination. Strengthen the future by making belonging and responsibility more explicit.","symbolism":"Pentacles arranged around the Gothic household connect personal effort to generations and a wider circle of care.","aff":["I help build a future others can inhabit."],"question":"What do you want your work to make possible beyond yourself?","image":"/cards/gothic/ten-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Ten of Pentacles: Pentacles arranged around the Gothic household connect personal effort to generations and a wider circle of care.","artStatus":"pending"},{"id":"page-of-pentacles","n":74,"rn":"Page","name":"Page of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["study","opportunity","apprenticeship"],"up":"Meet a practical ambition as a student. Learn the basics, make a manageable plan, and give consistent attention to the first task.","rev":"Procrastination or idealized plans may be delaying useful learning. Make the next step small enough to do today.","symbolism":"The young bearer studies the pentacle closely, finding wonder in something concrete and workable.","aff":["I can learn by beginning with what is in my hands."],"question":"What basic skill would move your intention closer to reality?","image":"/cards/gothic/page-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Page of Pentacles: The young bearer studies the pentacle closely, finding wonder in something concrete and workable.","artStatus":"pending"},{"id":"knight-of-pentacles","n":75,"rn":"Knight","name":"Knight of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["reliability","method","perseverance"],"up":"Keep faith with the useful routine. Dependable progress may be quiet, but it turns an intention into something others can trust.","rev":"Rigidity or stalled momentum may be hiding within diligence. Review whether the method still serves the goal.","symbolism":"The steady rider and held pentacle give patience a visible direction through the Gothic landscape.","aff":["I build trust through steady, thoughtful effort."],"question":"Which routine helps you progress, and which needs renewal?","image":"/cards/gothic/knight-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Knight of Pentacles: The steady rider and held pentacle give patience a visible direction through the Gothic landscape.","artStatus":"pending"},{"id":"queen-of-pentacles","n":76,"rn":"Queen","name":"Queen of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["nurture","resourcefulness","grounding"],"up":"Make care tangible through food, time, shelter, and thoughtful boundaries. Resourcefulness flourishes when your own needs are included.","rev":"Caring for everything may be leaving you depleted, or worry may be crowding out comfort. Restore your own base of support.","symbolism":"The queen's pentacle and living surroundings join practical skill with the care that makes a place habitable.","aff":["My practical care includes myself."],"question":"What would make your everyday environment more nourishing?","image":"/cards/gothic/queen-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"Queen of Pentacles: The queen's pentacle and living surroundings join practical skill with the care that makes a place habitable.","artStatus":"pending"},{"id":"king-of-pentacles","n":77,"rn":"King","name":"King of Pentacles","arcana":"Minor","suit":"Pentacles","keywords":["stewardship","stability","mastery"],"up":"Use experience and resources to create dependable conditions. Success becomes meaningful when it supports people and remains accountable.","rev":"Status, possessiveness, or inflexibility may be replacing good stewardship. Reconnect material choices with the wellbeing they should serve.","symbolism":"The pentacle sovereign's grounded throne represents responsibility for resources, continuity, and the lives supported by them.","aff":["I use stability to support a wider good."],"question":"How can what you have built become more useful and generous?","image":"/cards/gothic/king-of-pentacles.webp","alt":"King of Pentacles: The pentacle sovereign's grounded throne represents responsibility for resources, continuity, and the lives supported by them.","artStatus":"pending"}]});
